{"code":"29-2035.00","title":"Magnetic Resonance Imaging Technologists","description":"Operate Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI) scanners. Monitor patient safety and comfort, and view images of area being scanned to ensure quality of pictures. May administer gadolinium contrast dosage intravenously. May interview patient, explain MRI procedures, and position patient on examining table. May enter into the computer data such as patient history, anatomical area to be scanned, orientation specified, and position of entry.","jobZone":3,"kinds":{"R":{"score":5.46,"share":0.2981},"I":{"score":4.79,"share":0.2533},"A":{"score":1,"share":0},"S":{"score":3.51,"share":0.1678},"E":{"score":1.27,"share":0.018},"C":{"score":4.93,"share":0.2627}},"highPoints":["R","C","I"],"tasks":[{"id":19218,"text":"Conduct screening interviews of patients to identify contraindications, such as ferrous objects, pregnancy, prosthetic heart valves, cardiac pacemakers, or tattoos.","core":true,"importance":5,"relevance":100,"frequency":6.57},{"id":23974,"text":"Review physicians' orders to confirm prescribed exams.","core":true,"importance":5,"relevance":100,"frequency":6.67},{"id":19228,"text":"Select appropriate imaging techniques or coils to produce required images.","core":true,"importance":4.91,"relevance":100,"frequency":6.71},{"id":19225,"text":"Operate magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) scanners.","core":true,"importance":4.87,"relevance":100,"frequency":6.67},{"id":19227,"text":"Provide headphones or earplugs to patients to improve comfort and reduce unpleasant noise.","core":true,"importance":4.83,"relevance":100,"frequency":6.67},{"id":19233,"text":"Place and secure small, portable magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) scanners on body part to be imaged, such as arm, leg, or head.","core":false,"importance":4.79,"relevance":65.22,"frequency":6.54},{"id":19226,"text":"Position patients on cradle, attaching immobilization devices, if needed, to ensure appropriate placement for imaging.","core":tru